Firewall Rules
1️⃣ Allow outside hosts to access telnet only on 192.168.60.5
sudo iptables -A FORWARD -i br-288a365a777c -o br-c39f0aea5210 -p tcp -d 192.168.60.5 --dport 23 -j ACCEPT
2️⃣ Block outside hosts from accessing telnet on other internal hosts
sudo iptables -A FORWARD -i br-288a365a777c -o br-c39f0aea5210 -p tcp --dport 23 -j DROP
3️⃣ Allow internal hosts to access all internal servers
sudo iptables -A FORWARD -i br-c39f0aea5210 -o br-c39f0aea5210 -j ACCEPT
4️⃣ Block internal hosts from accessing external servers
sudo iptables -A FORWARD -i br-c39f0aea5210 -o br-288a365a777c -j DROP
5️⃣ Allow return traffic
sudo iptables -A FORWARD -p tcp --sport 23 -j ACCEPT
6️⃣ Default policy
sudo iptables -P FORWARD DROP
What these rules enforce
Traffic	Result
Outside → 192.168.60.5 telnet	✅ Allowed
Outside → other internal telnet servers	❌ Blocked
Internal → internal servers	✅ Allowed
Internal → external servers	❌ Blocked
Reset firewall (as required by lab)

After finishing the exercise:

sudo iptables -F
sudo iptables -P OUTPUT ACCEPT
sudo iptables -P INPUT ACCEPT
sudo iptables -P FORWARD ACCEPT
